<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- The mod's variant of vanilla CutoutComplex, used only by the two warcasket uniques in this
       compat root, whose masks have feathered red|green edges. Every other unique keeps vanilla
       CutoutComplex, where hard-edged masks render identically.
       Same properties, tags and pass state as vanilla, one difference: the two mask tints are
       MIXED (r*one + g*two + (1-r-g)) instead of stacked (lerp(1,one,r) * lerp(1,two,g)), so a
       feathered or anti-aliased red|green mask edge renders the blend the artist painted rather
       than a lighter product. Pure red, pure green and black texels are bit-identical to vanilla,
       so art needs no change. Source: Source/UnityShaders/ (built per OS into this root's
       AssetBundles/, so neither these defs nor the bundles load without VFE Pirates:
       ModAssetBundlesHandler walks every active load root, like Defs).

       ShaderDatabase resolves shaderPath in Resources first, then in the mod's asset bundles at
       Assets/Data/shunter.uniquemeleeweapons/Materials/<shaderPath>.shader. Both paths here are
       mirrored as constants in Patches/ShaderDatabase_LoadShader_Fallback_Patch.cs (applied only
       while VFE Pirates is active), which makes a missing or unsupported shader degrade to vanilla
       CutoutComplex (+ its UI twin) instead of plain Cutout, and fixes the stale-cache drop after
       a mid-session language change. Change a path here, in that patch, and in the Unity project
       together. -->
  <ShaderTypeDef>
    <defName>UMW_CutoutComplexMix</defName>
    <shaderPath>UMW/CutoutComplexMix</shaderPath>
    <uiShaderPath>UMW/CutoutComplexMixUI</uiShaderPath>
  </ShaderTypeDef>

</Defs>
